# Test video. `assets/videos/` was untracked but *not* ignored, so a `git add -A`
# would have staged a 170 MB clip — and GitHub refuses anything over 100 MB only
# after the commit exists, which is the expensive place to find out. Video is the one
# asset kind here that is routinely too big to track; keep clips local and name them
# in the recipe instead.
#
# `assets/videos/*`, not `assets/videos/` — git cannot re-include a file whose
# *parent directory* is excluded, so the negation below is silently dead with the
# directory form. Matching the contents instead keeps it live.
assets/videos/*
# ...except the test fixture, which exists to be committed: 2.9 KB, 128x64, 24
# frames, cut down from `2d_test_sample.mp4`. It is a *2D* clip used as a 360
# source, so it is geometrically nonsense on a sphere — irrelevant to what the
# tests read from it, which is only whether playback starts.
!assets/videos/tiny_test.mp4

# cargo artifacts in patched crates
patches/**/.cargo-ok
patches/**/.cargo_vcs_info.json
patches/**/Cargo.toml.orig
patches/**/Cargo.lock

# android/quest build outputs and fetched binaries
android/quest/build/
android/quest/jni/
android/quest/libs/**/*.so

# `crates/xrds-audio` is excluded from the workspace (deprecated), so building it by hand
# generates its own lockfile. Not worth tracking for a crate slated for deletion.
crates/xrds-audio/Cargo.lock

# Portable assessment kit (built artifacts; see examples/assessment/README.md)
/dist/
